In a discussion on creating a custom legend in RShiny using `addLegend_decreasing`, James faced issues with colors not appearing in the legend. Initial attempts using a function showed only dashes instead of colors. I suggested refinements to ensure correct color generation and formatting without concatenating color strings. Despite adjustments, colors displayed correctly but the legend did not appear. We then confirmed a simplified call of `addLegend` worked but displayed increasing order (negatives on top). To achieve a decreasing order, I recommended reversing the limits for the color palette and updating the values supplied to `addLegend`. This solution aimed to position higher values at the top, providing a clear gradient representation.
